# Local length formula for principal orders

At a codimension-one point of an integral locally Noetherian scheme, a nonzero element of the
local ring determines an element of the function field. This file identifies its scheme-theoretic
order, and hence its coefficient in the principal divisor, with the finite length of the local
ring modulo the generated principal ideal. This is the local algebra bridge needed to compare
principal-divisor coefficients with scheme-theoretic intersection multiplicities.
-/

